The wound was almost healed.

293
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:04,240
Then why did it tear open even more?

294
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:05,400
Huh?

295
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:07,120
What did you do?

296
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:13,240
And how is your boyfriend doing?

297
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:15,240
Why do you even want to know?

298
00:19:17,840 --> 00:19:18,600
I know

299
00:19:19,440 --> 00:19:20,880
that whatever I say,

300
00:19:21,120 --> 00:19:22,600
I can't order you around anyway.

301
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:27,920
But you should stop living your life like this.

302
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:32,600
Is my life really that hard to understand?

303
00:19:33,080 --> 00:19:34,160
It's not normal!

304
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:36,840
But I chose this path myself.

305
00:19:37,560 --> 00:19:38,960
You know how I grew up.

306
00:19:45,280 --> 00:19:46,360
I understand,

307
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:48,720
but others don't, do they?

308
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:50,160
Right?

309
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:51,760
Do you even realize that

310
00:19:51,760 --> 00:19:53,120
on the day you got shot,

311
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,680
your boyfriend was worried sick about you?

312
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,520
If you don't care about yourself,

313
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:01,600
at least care about the people who love you.

314
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:36,200
Hey.

315
00:20:41,360 --> 00:20:42,200
What are you doing?

316
00:20:43,120 --> 00:20:43,960
Working.

317
00:20:57,080 --> 00:20:57,880
P'Jane...

318
00:20:59,080 --> 00:21:00,080
P'Jane...

319
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:02,480
I'm not in the mood.

320
00:21:35,440 --> 00:21:36,920
Please, can you not?

321
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:39,160
I'm really not in the mood right now.

322
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:50,120
This weekend, I'd like to go back

323
00:21:50,120 --> 00:21:51,280
and stay with my family.

324
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:00,920
Of course.

325
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:46,960
Jane,

326
00:22:49,800 --> 00:22:50,600
are you asleep yet?

327
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:00,480
What is it?

328
00:23:02,760 --> 00:23:04,120
There's something I want to ask.

329
00:23:07,280 --> 00:23:08,280
I want to know,

330
00:23:08,840 --> 00:23:10,880
when we first agreed to date,

331
00:23:12,920 --> 00:23:15,120
what kind of life together did you imagine?

332
00:23:31,600 --> 00:23:33,520
I never liked anything flashy.

333
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:36,000
Do you know

334
00:23:37,640 --> 00:23:39,320
that my happiest day

335
00:23:41,440 --> 00:23:42,800
wasn't the day you closed down a whole restaurant

336
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:45,040
to surprise me for Valentine's Day.

337
00:23:51,480 --> 00:23:52,760
Then which day was it?

338
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:57,400
It was the day you went to see my family

339
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:00,600
to prove

340
00:24:01,960 --> 00:24:03,360
that you were sincere about me.

341
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:07,160
That day,

342
00:24:09,320 --> 00:24:11,400
you tried to help me with everything.

343
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:16,080
You were so clumsy, you know.

344
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:22,040
I felt like

345
00:24:24,080 --> 00:24:26,200
I was one of the very few people

346
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:30,000
who got to see that side of you.

347
00:24:35,600 --> 00:24:37,200
The side where you weren't some superhero,

348
00:24:40,040 --> 00:24:41,600
or a demon

349
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:44,800
that people rumored you to be.

350
00:24:50,080 --> 00:24:51,760
Do you like seeing me like that?

351
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:56,480
Just having ordinary days together,

352
00:24:59,760 --> 00:25:01,680
having times where we can laugh.

353
00:25:06,960 --> 00:25:08,160
But I also know

354
00:25:10,240 --> 00:25:12,240
that you don't want that kind of life.

355
00:25:15,840 --> 00:25:17,160
So I realized...

356
00:25:20,680 --> 00:25:22,480
maybe we're just too different.

357
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:15,240
Go to sleep.

358
00:26:44,480 --> 00:26:47,080
(Thanapat Piboonosot)

359
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:50,000
Oh, Jane,

360
00:26:50,680 --> 00:26:52,080
you're back just in time.

361
00:26:54,440 --> 00:26:55,280
Great,

362
00:26:55,600 --> 00:26:57,440
we can all have dinner together.

363
00:26:59,040 --> 00:27:00,800
Is there anything special you want to eat?

364
00:27:05,680 --> 00:27:06,640
Anything is fine.

365
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:17,560
Is something wrong

366
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:19,600
with him?

367
00:27:21,440 --> 00:27:22,240
Yeah, I wonder.

368
00:27:43,240 --> 00:27:44,760
Want some stir-fried veggies?

369
00:27:44,760 --> 00:27:46,240
Eat up, eat a lot.

370
00:27:46,240 --> 00:27:46,960
Ah..

371
00:27:46,960 --> 00:27:49,600
No more, I can't finish it all.

372
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:52,000
Want an omelet?

373
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:53,640
I can fry one up for you.

374
00:27:56,920 --> 00:27:57,720
Uh,

375
00:27:58,320 --> 00:27:59,000
and...

376
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:00,560
didn't your boyfriend drop you off today?

377
00:28:02,440 --> 00:28:03,080
Huh?

378
00:28:03,840 --> 00:28:04,800
Why did you ask that?

379
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:14,760
I'm full.

380
00:28:15,120 --> 00:28:15,800
Hey...

381
00:28:35,800 --> 00:28:37,760
Do you have any idea how worried I was?

382
00:28:39,160 --> 00:28:40,920
Can you please stop living your life like this?

383
00:28:42,600 --> 00:28:43,520
I can't stop.

384
00:28:44,520 --> 00:28:46,080
I've come too far to turn back.

385
00:28:47,520 --> 00:28:48,680
It's my life.

386
00:28:54,600 --> 00:28:56,800
How do you think I can bear it?

387
00:28:57,560 --> 00:28:58,600
Having to see you live

388
00:28:58,600 --> 00:28:59,680
like this every single day.

389
00:29:00,840 --> 00:29:01,840
That's exactly why I didn't want to

390
00:29:01,840 --> 00:29:03,200
involve you in any of this.

391
00:29:16,760 --> 00:29:18,200
If you choose this kind of life,

392
00:29:19,560 --> 00:29:21,560
I wish you the best of luck then.

393
00:29:50,400 --> 00:29:51,280
Hi P'Put.

394
00:29:51,800 --> 00:29:52,600
Hello.

395
00:29:53,080 --> 00:29:54,080
What are you doing here?

396
00:29:55,400 --> 00:29:56,480
Is Jane home.

397
00:30:00,880 --> 00:30:01,880
He's not.

398
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:06,480
Ah ok, thanks.

399
00:30:06,800 --> 00:30:07,600
Sure.

400
00:30:23,600 --> 00:30:27,800
(Put: I'm really sorry about that day.)

401
00:31:16,560 --> 00:31:17,160
Hi.

402
00:31:17,160 --> 00:31:18,160
Today, we're going to show you

403
00:31:18,160 --> 00:31:19,960
how to make ginkgo nuts in syrup.

404
00:31:19,960 --> 00:31:21,760
There are only a few ingredients.

405
00:31:21,760 --> 00:31:24,280
Brown sugar, pandan leaves,

406
00:31:24,280 --> 00:31:25,880
and boiled ginkgo nuts.

407
00:31:25,880 --> 00:31:27,680
We will bring the water to a boil.

408
00:31:27,680 --> 00:31:28,760
Once the water is boiling,

409
00:31:28,760 --> 00:31:30,400
we will add the brown sugar.

410
00:31:31,880 --> 00:31:33,000
And most importantly,

411
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:35,000
pandan leaves to add a nice aroma.

412
00:31:35,920 --> 00:31:36,920
When the sugar dissolves,

413
00:31:36,920 --> 00:31:38,880
we will add the boiled ginkgo nuts.

414
00:31:39,480 --> 00:31:40,040
After that,

415
00:31:40,040 --> 00:31:42,040
we'll let it simmer for about five minutes.

416
00:31:42,040 --> 00:31:43,760
We can put the lid on and wait.

417
00:31:46,400 --> 00:31:47,880
Here it is, our ginkgo nuts in syrup.

418
00:31:47,880 --> 00:31:49,680
Be sure to give this recipe a try.

419
00:33:04,040 --> 00:33:08,600
(Caption: Or maybe we're just too different)

420
00:34:06,680 --> 00:34:08,880
(Gap)

421
00:34:17,800 --> 00:34:18,600
Hello?

422
00:34:19,679 --> 00:34:20,480
Hello, Jane?

423
00:34:21,080 --> 00:34:22,600
Get to the hospital right now.

424
00:34:22,600 --> 00:34:24,080
Put is in the ER room right now.

425
00:34:24,560 --> 00:34:25,600
He's in critical condition.

426
00:34:30,199 --> 00:34:31,560
Yeah, I'll be right there.

427
00:34:48,159 --> 00:34:48,960
What happened to Put?

428
00:34:54,120 --> 00:34:54,639
Well...

429
00:34:55,480 --> 00:34:56,800
Put was riding his big bike,

430
00:34:57,880 --> 00:34:59,040
and a speeding car swerved

431
00:34:59,040 --> 00:35:00,040
into his lane and hit him.

432
00:35:01,400 --> 00:35:02,960
They said it looked like a luxury car.

433
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:06,360
Must be some rich kid for sure.

434
00:35:09,280 --> 00:35:11,680
The bastard even did a hit-and-run.

435
00:35:13,400 --> 00:35:14,640
They can't track them down.

436
00:35:16,560 --> 00:35:17,480
And...

437
00:35:17,480 --> 00:35:20,200
Put's family went to work out of town,

438
00:35:20,880 --> 00:35:22,560
but I've called and told them all.

439
00:35:22,880 --> 00:35:25,280
They're on their way and should be here soon.

440
00:35:32,560 --> 00:35:34,080
Who is Jenalee?

441
00:35:38,360 --> 00:35:39,160
I am.

442
00:35:40,280 --> 00:35:41,760
The patient asked to see you.

443
00:35:42,960 --> 00:35:45,160
The patient is still conscious right now,

444
00:35:47,720 --> 00:35:50,200
but it might not be for much longer.

445
00:35:54,920 --> 00:35:55,920
This way, please.

446
00:36:13,440 --> 00:36:14,320
Right this way.

447
00:36:26,600 --> 00:36:27,400
Put...

448
00:36:30,560 --> 00:36:31,360
Put...

449
00:36:37,440 --> 00:36:38,840
Hang in there a bit longer.

450
00:36:41,840 --> 00:36:43,680
Your family is on their way.

451
00:36:52,280 --> 00:36:53,120
I'm...

452
00:36:54,520 --> 00:36:55,360
sorry.

453
00:37:00,680 --> 00:37:01,480
P'...

454
00:37:01,800 --> 00:37:02,600
Jane.

455
00:37:06,480 --> 00:37:07,880
What did you say?

456
00:37:09,840 --> 00:37:11,480
P'Jane...

457
00:37:21,280 --> 00:37:22,800
What about P'Jane, Put?

458
00:37:23,680 --> 00:37:24,440
Put...

459
00:37:24,440 --> 00:37:25,280
What about P'Jane?

460
00:37:27,520 --> 00:37:28,320
Put...

461
00:37:30,280 --> 00:37:31,080
Put!

462
00:37:33,160 --> 00:37:34,280
Put!

463
00:37:36,960 --> 00:37:37,720
Doctor!

464
00:37:37,720 --> 00:37:38,360
Doctor!

465
00:37:38,360 --> 00:37:39,000
Doctor!

466
00:37:39,000 --> 00:37:40,320
Doctor, please help him!

467
00:37:40,320 --> 00:37:41,760
Please wait outside.

468
00:37:41,760 --> 00:37:42,520
Put!

469
00:37:44,920 --> 00:37:45,680
Please wait outside.

470
00:37:54,040 --> 00:37:54,640
Put...

471
00:38:17,440 --> 00:38:18,440
Jane,

472
00:38:18,440 --> 00:38:19,560
how is he, sweetie?

473
00:38:19,960 --> 00:38:20,600
Auntie...

474
00:38:20,800 --> 00:38:22,680
Jane, you went in to see Put, right?

475
00:38:22,680 --> 00:38:24,160
How is he? Huh?

476
00:38:24,160 --> 00:38:25,120
How is he doing?

477
00:38:26,760 --> 00:38:27,560
Auntie...

478
00:38:31,320 --> 00:38:32,600
Put... he's... not with us anymore

479
00:38:45,960 --> 00:38:47,680
Auntie...

480
00:38:57,760 --> 00:38:59,520
It's not true, right?

481
00:38:59,520 --> 00:39:00,920
It's not true.

482
00:39:00,920 --> 00:39:02,480
It's not true, right?

483
00:39:03,120 --> 00:39:04,400
It's not true.

484
00:39:04,400 --> 00:39:05,920
I don't believe it.

485
00:39:05,920 --> 00:39:07,200
I don't believe it.

486
00:39:13,040 --> 00:39:14,120
Is it really true?

487
00:39:14,120 --> 00:39:15,400
No way.

488
00:39:16,280 --> 00:39:17,120
When I went inside,

489
00:39:17,120 --> 00:39:19,200
I didn't know what to say to him.

490
00:39:20,200 --> 00:39:21,080
I didn't even get to say

491
00:39:21,080 --> 00:39:23,080
a proper goodbye to him yet.

492
00:39:24,760 --> 00:39:26,960
Why did it happen so fast?

493
00:39:27,920 --> 00:39:30,640
You guys just made up not too long ago.

494
00:39:49,080 --> 00:39:49,600
Jane...

495
00:39:50,240 --> 00:39:51,840
I'm really sorry about just now.

496
00:39:52,040 --> 00:39:53,320
Argh! Hey!

497
00:39:54,080 --> 00:39:55,480
If you ever come near Jane again,

498
00:39:56,280 --> 00:39:57,720
I won't let you off easy.

499
00:40:00,520 --> 00:40:03,520
It's not true! It's not true!

500
00:40:05,120 --> 00:40:06,800
Jane?

501
00:40:36,480 --> 00:40:37,280
Okay.

502
00:40:38,080 --> 00:40:39,200
You did a great job.

503
00:40:41,560 --> 00:40:43,320
You got all the evidence clean, right?

504
00:40:45,680 --> 00:40:47,440
Then our favor is now concluded.

505
00:40:48,560 --> 00:40:50,720
Pleasure doing business with you.

506
00:41:07,560 --> 00:41:08,640
Jane, what are you doing?

507
00:41:09,240 --> 00:41:10,280
Why are you doing this?

508
00:41:12,480 --> 00:41:14,000
You killed Put, didn't you?

509
00:41:16,440 --> 00:41:17,800
Did you kill him?

510
00:41:22,160 --> 00:41:22,960
What happened?

511
00:41:24,480 --> 00:41:25,440
Put is dead?

512
00:41:29,880 --> 00:41:30,960
I know nothing about this.

513
00:41:35,440 --> 00:41:36,880
How can I trust you?

514
00:41:38,040 --> 00:41:40,240
How many times have you lied to me before?

515
00:41:41,080 --> 00:41:41,800
Besides,

516
00:41:43,440 --> 00:41:44,480
before he died,

517
00:41:44,920 --> 00:41:46,640
Put said your name.

518
00:41:48,240 --> 00:41:50,240
And on that day, you went and threatened him.

519
00:41:54,480 --> 00:41:55,880
If you don't believe me,

520
00:41:57,440 --> 00:41:58,760
you can go tell the police.

521
00:41:59,240 --> 00:41:59,800
I'm more than willing to

522
00:41:59,800 --> 00:42:01,120
let them fully investigate me.

523
00:42:01,120 --> 00:42:03,240
What can the police even do to someone like you?

524
00:42:15,800 --> 00:42:16,600
Jane...

525
00:42:19,760 --> 00:42:21,520
Can you please trust me just this once?

526
00:42:27,880 --> 00:42:28,720
Trust you?

527
00:42:32,880 --> 00:42:33,880
I can't handle this anymore.

528
00:42:35,120 --> 00:42:36,280
I can't handle this anymore, damn it!

529
00:42:36,920 --> 00:42:37,520
Do you hear me?

530
00:42:37,520 --> 00:42:38,840
I can't handle this anymore!

531
00:42:39,800 --> 00:42:41,840
I can't trust you anymore!

532
00:43:07,600 --> 00:43:09,680
I can't trust you anymore!

533
00:43:11,200 --> 00:43:13,320
Ever since you came into my life,

534
00:43:14,200 --> 00:43:16,200
everything has been completely ruined.

535
00:43:19,000 --> 00:43:21,360
I have nothing left, P'Jane.

536
00:43:52,960 --> 00:43:53,760
Jane...

537
00:44:02,800 --> 00:44:03,720
You're the person who gives anyone

538
00:44:03,720 --> 00:44:05,040
whatever they ask for, right?

539
00:44:21,520 --> 00:44:24,120
Then I'm asking you to disappear from my life.

540
00:44:51,280 --> 00:44:53,760
Are you fully in your right mind right now?

541
00:44:55,280 --> 00:44:55,960
Are you really insisting

542
00:44:55,960 --> 00:44:57,800
on making a contract with me?

543
00:44:59,520 --> 00:45:01,080
A contract where I can demand anything back

544
00:45:01,080 --> 00:45:02,680
from you in return.

545
00:45:07,160 --> 00:45:07,960
Yes.

546
00:45:21,960 --> 00:45:23,040
Then tonight,

547
00:45:25,440 --> 00:45:27,480
I ask to stay with you for one last night.

548
00:45:28,920 --> 00:45:30,440
And after this,

549
00:45:33,280 --> 00:45:35,600
I will disappear from your life.

550
00:45:38,520 --> 00:45:40,000
And we won't owe each other

551
00:45:40,000 --> 00:45:41,160
anything anymore, right?

552
00:45:53,720 --> 00:45:55,600
If that's what you want.

553
00:52:46,520 --> 00:52:47,880
Hello, Jane.

554
00:52:48,800 --> 00:52:50,840
I'm sorry for leaving without saying goodbye.

555
00:52:52,080 --> 00:52:53,800
But I didn't think I'd be strong enough

556
00:52:53,800 --> 00:52:55,240
to walk out of your life

557
00:52:55,640 --> 00:52:57,240
if you were still awake.

558
00:52:58,720 --> 00:53:01,160
The reason I had to leave this letter behind

559
00:53:02,400 --> 00:53:03,160
is because there's something

560
00:53:03,160 --> 00:53:04,360
I absolutely have to tell you.

561
00:53:05,400 --> 00:53:07,080
But I'm not good with words,

562
00:53:07,840 --> 00:53:09,720
which is why I have to write it down like this.

563
00:53:11,680 --> 00:53:13,400
The reason I chose to leave you

564
00:53:14,040 --> 00:53:15,680
isn't because I killed Put.

565
00:53:16,640 --> 00:53:17,960
I didn't do it.

566
00:53:19,000 --> 00:53:20,320
If you won't believe me,

567
00:53:20,800 --> 00:53:22,200
I understand,

568
00:53:22,840 --> 00:53:25,800
because everything I've done to you has been awful.

569
00:53:26,720 --> 00:53:27,400
And that is exactly

570
00:53:27,800 --> 00:53:29,800
the reason why I'm leaving you.

571
00:53:31,400 --> 00:53:32,640
I want you to be able to smile

572
00:53:32,640 --> 00:53:34,280
again like the old Jane,

573
00:53:34,280 --> 00:53:36,520
the one before you ever knew me.

574
00:53:36,520 --> 00:53:39,040
You might not trust me anymore,

575
00:53:39,040 --> 00:53:41,280
but there is one thing I want to reassure you

576
00:53:41,800 --> 00:53:43,960
I have never once lied to you.

577
00:53:44,360 --> 00:53:45,440
The part where I told you

578
00:53:45,440 --> 00:53:47,240
that you are special to me.

579
00:53:48,480 --> 00:53:50,720
You often think of yourself as ordinary,

580
00:53:51,680 --> 00:53:53,080
But you are is the most extraordinary

581
00:53:53,080 --> 00:53:55,880
ordinary person in the world to me.

582
00:53:58,720 --> 00:54:00,520
So, I want to tell you ten reasons

583
00:54:00,520 --> 00:54:02,880
that make me think you are so very special.

584
00:54:04,640 --> 00:54:06,040
First,

585
00:54:06,040 --> 00:54:07,960
everyone who knows me

586
00:54:07,960 --> 00:54:08,960
either wants something from me

587
00:54:08,960 --> 00:54:10,880
or looks at me like a demon.

588
00:54:10,880 --> 00:54:11,840
But just looking into your eyes,

589
00:54:11,840 --> 00:54:13,800
I knew you were the first person

590
00:54:13,800 --> 00:54:16,560
who didn't judge me from our very first meeting.

591
00:54:16,560 --> 00:54:18,840
Second,

592
00:54:18,840 --> 00:54:19,920
the way you get nervous

593
00:54:19,920 --> 00:54:21,920
when dancing with me is so cute.

594
00:54:22,640 --> 00:54:24,240
No matter how many dozens of times

595
00:54:24,240 --> 00:54:26,080
you step on my feet,

596
00:54:26,080 --> 00:54:28,000
I don't mind.

597
00:54:29,040 --> 00:54:30,680
Third,

598
00:54:30,680 --> 00:54:33,640
you changed my mind about a lot of things.

599
00:54:33,640 --> 00:54:34,920
You made me believe that this world

600
00:54:34,920 --> 00:54:36,560
still has people who want to strive

601
00:54:36,560 --> 00:54:38,000
and do things on their own.

602
00:54:38,600 --> 00:54:39,680
Fourth,

603
00:54:40,040 --> 00:54:41,600
I never liked taking photos,

604
00:54:42,440 --> 00:54:43,480
but you made me willing to

605
00:54:43,480 --> 00:54:44,680
take photos with you.

606
00:54:45,360 --> 00:54:47,560
I wanted to have photos of us together,

607
00:54:47,560 --> 00:54:50,160
wanted to declare that you belong to me alone.

608
00:54:51,520 --> 00:54:52,320
Fifth,

609
00:54:53,600 --> 00:54:55,480
I don't care how anyone else looks at me,

610
00:54:56,000 --> 00:54:56,800
except for you.

611
00:54:57,480 --> 00:54:59,640
You were willing to fight with your friends for me,

612
00:55:00,120 --> 00:55:01,400
so I wanted to prove myself

613
00:55:01,400 --> 00:55:03,200
to you and your family.

614
00:55:04,280 --> 00:55:05,000
Sixth,

615
00:55:05,760 --> 00:55:07,520
you said I make you happy

616
00:55:07,520 --> 00:55:09,400
when we're together.

617
00:55:09,400 --> 00:55:12,000
I'm happy when I'm with you too.

618
00:55:12,960 --> 00:55:13,840
Seventh,

619
00:55:14,760 --> 00:55:15,800
you made me realize that

620
00:55:15,800 --> 00:55:17,760
things made from the heart

621
00:55:17,760 --> 00:55:18,680
are much more important than

622
00:55:18,680 --> 00:55:20,480
countless luxury items.

623
00:55:20,480 --> 00:55:22,480
So I wanted to make something simple

624
00:55:22,880 --> 00:55:24,880
but made from the heart for you to eat.

625
00:55:27,680 --> 00:55:28,720
Eighth,

626
00:55:29,480 --> 00:55:31,920
you worry about me and take care of me,

627
00:55:31,920 --> 00:55:34,080
both by bringing me Chinese medicine

628
00:55:34,080 --> 00:55:35,680
and helping tend to my wounds.

629
00:55:36,800 --> 00:55:38,080
Ninth,

630
00:55:38,080 --> 00:55:40,200
